	(gr_text "xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\nI'm Lander03xD. I make keyboards as a hobby and have made a good amount already. I started with handwiring keyboards when I first got my 3D printer, but \nquickly moved over to my own keyboard designs. I now design my own PCBs. I started working with QMK and later focussed more on ZMK because wireless keyboards \nare a lot better! FIGHT ME! I generally don't put RGB backlights on my keyboards because I rather have good battery life than flashy colors. You may not know \nthis yet, but RGB doesn't really give you extra FPS. Sorry to kill that dream. Now go download some more RAM! I stream all of my keyboard work and am \ndefinitely willing to help with any questions you have. This keyboard is the {dblquote}Low3xD{dblquote} keyboard because it sounds like 03xD and it's a low profile keyboard \ndesign. Yes, I'm very creative! I tried to include the 03xD into my keyboard names to link all the boards together a bit. Making keyboards isn't always a \nsmooth ride. I tend to make mistakes but there is always a solution. Fingers crossed this one is a design without any mistakes! If everything goes to plan \nand no big mistakes were made I'd like to send this to a friend for her to solder the board. Mangokeebs, if you read this, I'm talking about you! She's given \nmy some suggestions on which switches to use and my colleagues appreciated her silent switch suggestions a lot! This is the successor of my first PCB \nsandwich. My first PCB sandwich was the Direct03xD. I got this name because it was the first keyboard that I made with direct pin wiring. Fun fact,.. I'm \nwriting this text with the Direct03xD keyboard. I made the Direct03xD as a 42 key keyboard because I needed an extra column. I wanted to use the keyboard for \nsome stenography practice aswell. In normal typing I didn't use the extra keys and wanted to correct the mistakes I made in that board this time around. This \nis why the Low3xD is back at 36 keys. \n\nIk ben Lander03xD. Als hobby maak ik toetsenborden en heb er al een goed aantal gemaakt. Ik begon met handwiring toetsenborden toen ik mijn printer kocht, maar \nging al snel over naar mijn eigen designs. Nu design ik mijn eigen PCBs. Ik begon met QMK en focuste me later meer op ZMK omdat draadloos beter is! FIGHT ME! \nIk voeg normaal geen RGB backlights toe aan mijn toetsenborden omdat ik liever een langere batterijduur heb dan opvallende kleuren."
		(at 111.935 74.42 0)
		(layer "F.SilkS")
		(uuid "886a7f16-517e-481b-927a-24cc77628279")
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Ubuntu Mono")
				(size 1 1)
				(thickness 0.125)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(render_cache "xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\nI'm Lander03xD. I make keyboards as a hobby and have made a good amount already. I started with handwiring keyboards when I first got my 3D printer, but \nquickly moved over to my own keyboard designs. I now design my own PCBs. I started working with QMK and later focussed more on ZMK because wireless keyboards \nare a lot better! FIGHT ME! I generally don't put RGB backlights on my keyboards because I rather have good battery life than flashy colors. You may not know \nthis yet, but RGB doesn't really give you extra FPS. Sorry to kill that dream. Now go download some more RAM! I stream all of my keyboard work and am \ndefinitely willing to help with any questions you have. This keyboard is the \"Low3xD\" keyboard because it sounds like 03xD and it's a low profile keyboard \ndesign. Yes, I'm very creative! I tried to include the 03xD into my keyboard names to link all the boards together a bit. Making keyboards isn't always a \nsmooth ride. I tend to make mistakes but there is always a solution. Fingers crossed this one is a design without any mistakes! If everything goes to plan \nand no big mistakes were made I'd like to send this to a friend for her to solder the board. Mangokeebs, if you read this, I'm talking about you! She's given \nmy some suggestions on which switches to use and my colleagues appreciated her silent switch suggestions a lot! This is the successor of my first PCB \nsandwich. My first PCB sandwich was the Direct03xD. I got this name because it was the first keyboard that I made with direct pin wiring. Fun fact,.. I'm \nwriting this text with the Direct03xD keyboard. I made the Direct03xD as a 42 key keyboard because I needed an extra column. I wanted to use the keyboard for \nsome stenography practice aswell. In normal typing I didn't use the extra keys and wanted to correct the mistakes I made in that board this time around. This \nis why the Low3xD is back at 36 keys. \n\nIk ben Lander03xD. Als hobby maak ik toetsenborden en heb er al een goed aantal gemaakt. Ik begon met handwiring toetsenborden toen ik mijn printer kocht, maar \nging al snel over naar mijn eigen designs. Nu design ik mijn eigen PCBs. Ik begon met QMK en focuste me later meer op ZMK omdat draadloos beter is! FIGHT ME! \nIk voeg normaal geen RGB backlights toe aan mijn toetsenborden omdat ik liever een langere batterijduur heb dan opvallende kleuren."
